ting all potential tools before making calls. I'm focusing on alternatives to 'cat,' 'grep,' 'ls,' and 'sed,' prioritizing specialized utilities.\n\n\n"}
{"step_index":106,"source":"USER_EXPLICIT","type":"USER_INPUT","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-09-23T18:49:59Z","content":"<USER_REQUEST>\nI want to rebuild the frontend to function like a scientific space debris risk calculator, similar in structure to Calcimator, but using our premium, cinematic dark-mode Tailwind CSS styling.\n\nPlease update index.html and app.js with the following requirements:\n\nTwo-Column Grid Layout: Create a responsive grid. The left column will be the 'Mission Parameters' (Inputs), and the right column will be the 'Risk Assessment' (Outputs).\n\nInput Controls (Left Panel): Build a sleek form using glassmorphism (bg-black/40, backdrop-blur-md, thin borders). Include these input fields with clean labels and sliders (range inputs):\n\nTarget Altitude (km)\n\nSpacecraft Cross-Sectional Area (m²)\n\nTime in Orbit (years)\n\nAdd a prominent, glowing 'Calculate Risk' button.\n\nDynamic Results (Right Panel): Create a results dashboard that displays:\n\n'Probability of Impact': A large, glowing percentage number.\n\n'Risk Level': A dynamic badge (Green/Yellow/Red).\n\n'Risk Meter': A visual progress bar or gauge filling up based on the percentage.\n\nVanilla JS Logic: Write JavaScript to listen to the 'Calculate Risk' button. When clicked, read the input values, perform a basic mock calculation (e.g., higher altitude and longer time = higher risk percentage), and dynamically update the DOM elements in the right panel with the new numbers and colors.\n\nPremium Styling: Keep the SpaceX-style cinematic space background. Use sleek sans-serif typography, neon accents for active inputs, and ensure smooth CSS transitions when the results update.\n\nAction: Write the updated HTML, CSS, and JS. Once running, use your embedded browser to input some test numbers, click calculate, and take a full-screen screenshot of the active results for me to review.\"\n</USER_REQUEST>\n<ADDITIONAL_METADATA>\nThe current local time is: 2026-09-24T00:19:59+05:30.\n</ADDITIONAL_METADATA>"}
