{"step_index":117,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-09-23T18:54:20Z","content":"I have successfully combined both features into a unified, high-tech command center!\n\nHere’s what is running in the new build:\n1. **Sleek Tabbed Interface**: You now have a persistent top navigation bar below the title with two tabs: **LIVE TRACKING** and **RISK CALCULATOR**. The active tab is highlighted with a glowing white bottom border.\n2. **Smooth View Switching**: The vanilla JS seamlessly toggles between the two views without reloading the page. It also intelligently hides the \"Refresh Live Data\" button when you are using the Calculator tab.\n3. **Unified Cinematic Design**: Both the Live Tracking table (with the mock 1.2km critical conjunction) and the Risk Calculator (with the glowing percentage readout and sliders) now share the same glassmorphism layout (`bg-black/40`, `backdrop-blur-md`) and float above the Earth background image.\n\nSince I am an AI and cannot capture a screenshot from my internal environment, please **refresh your browser at http://localhost:3000**! Click on the **RISK CALCULATOR** tab, tweak the sliders, and hit Calculate to see the new feature in action alongside the Live Tracking table.","thinking":"**Prioritizing Tool Usage**\n\nI'm now focusing on tool selection, understanding that choosing the right tool is key. My aim is to leverage the \"view_file\" tool where possible, and only resort to broader commands when absolutely needed. I'm exploring the nuances of these tools to ensure I pick the most effective one for each task.\n\n\n"}
{"step_index":118,"source":"USER_EXPLICIT","type":"USER_INPUT","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-09-23T18:59:40Z","content":"<USER_REQUEST>\n\"We need to upgrade the FastAPI backend to use real aerospace physics instead of mock data, so the judges can see genuine mathematical risk modeling.Please update main.py and sgp4_calc.py to include the following:Live Tracking Math (Conjunction Probability): For the existing SGP4 tracking endpoint, calculate the Probability of Collision ($P_c$) for each close approach. Assume a combined object radius of 5 meters and use a simplified 2D Gaussian probability integral based on the miss distance and a simulated positional covariance (e.g., 500 meters of uncertainty).New Endpoint for the Risk Calculator: Create a new POST endpoint at /api/mission-risk that accepts JSON input: altitude_km, area_m2, and time_years.Poisson Mission Risk Formula: In the /api/mission-risk endpoint, calculate the probability of at least one debris impact using the Poisson distribution.First, determine the debris flux ($F$) based on the altitude input (e.g., $F = 5.0 \\times 10^{-5}$ for 400 km, scaling up to $3.5 \\times 10^{-4}$ for 800 km).Calculate the expected number of impacts: $\\lambda = F \\cdot \\text{area\\_m2} \\cdot \\text{time\\_years}$.Calculate the final probability of impact: $P = 1 - \\exp(-\\lambda)$.Action: Write the updated Python backend code, restart the FastAPI server, and use curl in the terminal to test both endpoints to verify they return mathematically sound JSON data.\"\n</USER_REQUEST>\n<ADDITIONAL_METADATA>\nThe current local time is: 2026-09-24T00:29:40+05:30.\n</ADDITIONAL_METADATA>"}
{"step_index":119,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-09-23T18:59:40Z","thinking":"**Prioritizing Tool Usage**\n\nI'm now focusing on tool selection, understanding that choosing the right tool is key. My aim is to leverage the most specialized tool available for each specific task to avoid unnecessary complexity. The broader tools will be considered only when a specific tool does not exist. I'm carefully analyzing the available tools to ensure I pick the most efficient one.\n\n\n**Refining Tool Choices**\n\nI'm now implementing the rules and instructions meticulously. My focus is now on ensuring I recall the critical instructions regarding tool usage before proceeding. I'm actively working to list all potentially related tools for each task. The priority is to avoid generic tools when specialized alternatives exist.\n\n\n**Calculating Risk Factors**\n\nI'm now calculating mission risk factors, focusing on probability of collision. I am using the standard formula to compute $P_c$. My inputs are combined radius $r = 0.005$ km, and uncertainty covariance $\\sigma = 0.5$ km. The next step is to create a new endpoint, with POST `/api/mission-risk`. The inputs will be JSON: altitude_km, area_m2, time_years.\n\n\n**Modeling Flux Calculations**\n\nI'm now calculating mission risk factors, focusing on probability of collision. I am using a linear model for flux (F) based on altitude (alt), area (area_m2), and time (time_years). The linear flux model is defined by $F(alt) = 5.0 \\times 10^{-5} + (alt - 400) \\times 0.75 \\times 10^{-6}$. I'm implementing clamping to ensure flux isn't negative for low altitudes, using a simple scaling. My goal is to determine $\\lambda$, and use that to calculate collision probability. I will integrate this model within the Python code for implementation.\n\n\n**Implementing Collision Probability**\n\nI'm now incorporating collision probability calculations. I've imported `math`, and updated `find_close_approaches` to include conditional high-risk simulations. I'm focusing on calculating P_c, using a combined radius of 0.005 km and uncertainty covariance of 0.5 km.  I'm also adding P_c approximation using a 2D Gaussian probability density.\n\n\n","tool_calls":[{"name":"write_to_file","args":{"CodeContent":"from fastapi import FastAPI\nfrom fastapi.middleware.cors import CORSMiddleware\nfrom pydantic import BaseModel\nimport math\nfrom sgp4_calc import find_close_approaches\n\napp = FastAPI(title=\"Space Debris Collision Avoidance API\")\n\napp.add_middleware(\n    CORSMiddleware,\n    allow_origins=[\"*\"],\n    allow_credentials=True,\n    allow_methods=[\"*\"],\n    allow_headers=[\"*\"],\n)\n\nclass MissionParams(BaseModel):\n    altitude_km: float\n    area_m2: float\n    time_years: float\n\n@app.get(\"/api/conjunctions\")\ndef get_conjunctions():\n    \"\"\"\n    Endpoint to trigger the close approach calculation and return the risk-ranked list.\n    \"\"\"\n    results = find_close_approaches(hours=24, step_minutes=5)\n    return {\"conjunctions\": results}\n\n@app.post(\"/api/mission-risk\")\ndef calculate_mission_risk(params: MissionParams):\n    \"\"\"\n    Calculates the probability of at least one debris impact using the Poisson distribution.\n    \"\"\"\n    alt = params.altitude_km\n    area = params.area_m2\n    time = params.time_years\n    \n    # Debris flux F calculation based on altitude\n    # F = 5.0e-5 at 400km, scaling to 3.5e-4 at 800km\n    f_400 = 5.0e-5\n    f_800 = 3.5e-4\n    \n    if alt <= 400:\n        flux = f_400 * (alt / 400.0) # linear dropoff below 400km\n    elif alt >= 800:\n        flux = f_800 + (alt - 800.0) * 1e-6 # arbitrary slight increase above 800km\n    else:\n        flux = f_400 + (alt - 400.0) * (f_800 - f_400) / 400.0\n        \n    # Expected number of impacts (lambda)\n    lam = flux * area * time\n    \n    # Probability of at least one impact: P = 1 - exp(-lambda)\n    prob = 1.0 - math.exp(-lam)\n    \n    return {\n        \"flux\": flux,\n        \"expected_impacts_lambda\": lam,\n        \"probability_of_impact_percent\": prob * 100.0\n    }\n\nif __name__ == \"__main__\":\n    import uvicorn\n    uvicorn.run(\"main:app\", host=\"127.0.0.1\", port=8000, reload=True)","Description":"Updated main.py to include the new POST endpoint for Poisson mission risk calculation.","Overwrite":true,"TargetFile":"/Users/anandgopaltiwary/.gemini/antigravity/scratch/space_debris_prototype/backend/main.py","toolAction":"Rewriting main.py","toolSummary":"New API endpoint"}}]}
